The paper does not claim an NP-hardness theorem; its main machinery is structural (single-arc flips, exact star formulas, and patterned grids). That makes a Track A claim untenable unless the generated distribution independently resists the standard domination algorithms. I’m now checking whether the star/grid constructions yield an honest Track B gap: huge generic subset enumeration versus a short structural extraction, without making the extraction itself obvious from the statement.
