We give a rigorous definition of this idea below, and we note that this definition holds for any orientation $\vec{G}$ of $G$.

\begin{defn} (\cite{harris2018broadcast})
A $(t,r)$ broadcast dominating set $S$ for $G$ is said to be \textbf{efficient} if for all $u \in V(G)$,
$$
r(u) = \begin{cases} 
r &\mbox{if } d(u,v) \geq t - r \text{ for all }v \in S \\

