Step 0 rules out a build. The strongest native, theorem-backed option is Proposition 3.14 on oriented stars: it gives a fixed 16-vertex minimum witness even as the star grows, but recovering that witness is exactly a linear scan for source leaves. On 1,000 randomly relabelled 4,096-vertex stars, the scan solved 1,000/1,000 with a 0.00319 s median; the supposed compact route must perform the same 4,095 direction inspections. I’m recording this, along with why the interval and grid theorems do not provide a harder witness family, in `REJECTED.md`.
